IMPORT prelude

-- Trade Marks Act 1998 (Singapore) -- what a trader meets: how long registration lasts (s 18), revocation for non-use
-- (s 22), infringement (s 27) and its exceptions (s 28), exhaustion and parallel imports (s 29), groundless threats (s 35),
-- and the counterfeiting offences (ss 46, 47, 49, 51).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TMA1998.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 23 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, thinly. SCOPED to the rights a
-- registration gives and the offences. Not encoded: application and examination, the absolute and relative grounds for
-- refusal (ss 7 to 9), priority, invalidity, trade marks as property and licensing, the Madrid Protocol and well-known marks
-- beyond s 27(3), collective and certification marks, border enforcement, and the Registry.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trade Marks Act 1998 -- rights and offences`

§§ `18, 22 -- duration, and losing the mark for non-use`

-- s 18: registered "for a period of 10 years", renewable for further periods of 10 years.
-- s 22(1)(a), (b): revocable if not put to genuine use in Singapore within 5 years after registration, or if use is
-- suspended for an uninterrupted 5 years, "and there are no proper reasons for non-use". (c): if it has become the common
-- name for the product through the proprietor's acts or inactivity. (d): if the proprietor's use makes it misleading.
-- (3): not revoked if use began or resumed after the 5 years but before the application -- but (4) use begun in the 3
-- months before the application is disregarded unless preparations began before the proprietor knew an application might
-- be made.
DECLARE Use HAS
    `years without genuine use` IS A NUMBER
    `proper reasons for non-use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `use resumed before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resumption was within 3 months before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `preparations began before the proprietor knew of a likely application` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resumption counts` IF
        `the use`'s `use resumed before the application`
    AND (    NOT `the use`'s `resumption was within 3 months before the application`
         OR  `the use`'s `preparations began before the proprietor knew of a likely application`)

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mark is liable to revocation for non-use` IF
        `the use`'s `years without genuine use` AT LEAST 5
    AND NOT `the use`'s `proper reasons for non-use`
    AND NOT `the resumption counts` `the use`

§§ `27, 28 -- infringement and its exceptions`

-- s 27(1): using in the course of trade, without consent, an IDENTICAL sign on IDENTICAL goods -- infringement, no confusion
-- needed. (2): identical sign on similar goods, or similar sign on identical or similar goods -- infringement only with "a
-- likelihood of confusion". (3): for a mark well known in Singapore, a similar sign on DISSIMILAR goods if it indicates a
-- connection, is likely to confuse, and is likely to damage the proprietor.
-- s 28(1): no infringement by honest use of one's own name, of descriptive indications, or to indicate intended purpose
-- (spare parts). (2): continuous prior use of an unregistered mark from before the registration or the proprietor's first use.
-- (4): "(a) fair use in comparative commercial advertising ...; (b) ... a NON-COMMERCIAL purpose; or (c) ... news reporting
-- or news commentary".
DECLARE Similarity IS ONE OF
    `identical`
    `similar`
    `dissimilar`

DECLARE UseFacts HAS
    `sign` IS A Similarity
    `goods` IS A Similarity
    `in the course of trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likelihood of confusion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mark is well known and the use damages and indicates a connection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 28 exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A UseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use infringes` IF
        `the facts`'s `in the course of trade`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `with consent`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `a section 28 exception applies`
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `sign`
        WHEN `dissimilar` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `identical` THEN
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `goods`
            WHEN `identical` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `similar` THEN `the facts`'s `likelihood of confusion`
            WHEN `dissimilar` THEN `the facts`'s `likelihood of confusion` AND `the facts`'s `the mark is well known and the use damages and indicates a connection`
        WHEN `similar` THEN
            CONSIDER `the facts`'s `goods`
            WHEN `dissimilar` THEN `the facts`'s `likelihood of confusion` AND `the facts`'s `the mark is well known and the use damages and indicates a connection`
            OTHERWISE `the facts`'s `likelihood of confusion`

DECLARE Exception IS ONE OF
    `honest use of one's own name`
    `honest descriptive use`
    `spare parts compatibility`
    `earlier continuous unregistered use`
    `fair comparative advertising`
    `non-commercial use`
    `news reporting`
    `a parody t-shirt sold for profit`

GIVEN `the exception` IS AN Exception
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exception is in section 28` IF
    CONSIDER `the exception`
    WHEN `a parody t-shirt sold for profit` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `29 -- parallel imports`

-- s 29(1): no infringement by use "in relation to goods which have been put on the market, whether in Singapore OR OUTSIDE
-- SINGAPORE, under that trade mark by the proprietor ... or with the proprietor's express or implied consent". (2): unless
-- "(a) the condition of the goods has been changed or impaired ... AND (b) the use ... has caused dilution in an unfair manner".
--
-- Singapore has international exhaustion: genuine goods bought cheaply abroad may be imported and sold here. The exception
-- needs BOTH changed condition AND unfair dilution; repackaged goods that cause no dilution remain lawful.
DECLARE Import HAS
    `genuine goods put on the market abroad by or with the proprietor's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `condition changed or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `causes unfair dilution` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the import` IS AN Import
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parallel import is lawful` IF
        `the import`'s `genuine goods put on the market abroad by or with the proprietor's consent`
    AND NOT (`the import`'s `condition changed or impaired` AND `the import`'s `causes unfair dilution`)

§§ `35 -- groundless threats`

-- s 35(1): a person threatened with infringement proceedings may sue for a declaration, injunction or damages -- EXCEPT
-- where the threat concerns "(a) the application of the mark to goods or ... packaging; (b) the importation of goods ...;
-- or (c) the supply of services under the mark". (3): relief unless the threatener proves infringement; (4) even then, if
-- the claimant shows the registration invalid or revocable. (5): mere notice of registration is not a threat. (6): an
-- advocate and solicitor acting for a client is not liable.
--
-- A proprietor can threaten a manufacturer or importer with impunity. Threatening a retailer who only sells is actionable
-- unless the threat is justified.
DECLARE Threatened IS ONE OF
    `a manufacturer applying the mark`
    `an importer`
    `a service provider using the mark`
    `a retailer who only sells`

GIVEN `the target` IS A Threatened, `the threatener proves infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threatened person has a remedy` IF
        NOT `the threatener proves infringement`
    AND CONSIDER `the target`
        WHEN `a retailer who only sells` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `46, 47, 49, 51 -- offences`

-- s 46: counterfeiting a registered mark -- $100,000 or 5 years; (3) the ACCUSED must prove the proprietor's consent.
-- s 47: falsely applying a mark, "unless the person proves that the person acted innocently" -- $100,000 or 5 years.
-- s 49: importing for trade, selling, or possessing for trade goods with a falsely applied mark, unless the person proves
-- reasonable precautions plus no reason to suspect plus full disclosure of suppliers, or innocence -- "$10,000 for EACH goods
-- or thing ... (but not exceeding in the aggregate $100,000) or ... 5 years".
-- s 51(1): falsely representing a mark as registered, knowing -- $10,000. (2): the word "registered", or ANY SYMBOL importing
-- registration (such as an R in a circle), is deemed a representation of SINGAPORE registration unless shown to refer to
-- registration elsewhere where the mark is in fact registered.
GIVEN `items` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for selling counterfeits` MEANS
    IF `items` TIMES 10000 GREATER THAN 100000 THEN 100000 ELSE `items` TIMES 10000

DECLARE Seller HAS
    `took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had no reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed all suppliers on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acted innocently` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the seller` IS A Seller
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller has a section 49 defence` IF
        (    `the seller`'s `took all reasonable precautions`
         AND `the seller`'s `had no reason to suspect`
         AND `the seller`'s `disclosed all suppliers on demand`)
    OR  `the seller`'s `acted innocently`

DECLARE RSymbol HAS
    `registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shown to refer to a foreign registration that exists` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or had reason to believe it was false` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the symbol` IS AN RSymbol
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the registered symbol is an offence` IF
        NOT `the symbol`'s `registered in Singapore`
    AND NOT `the symbol`'s `shown to refer to a foreign registration that exists`
    AND `the symbol`'s `knew or had reason to believe it was false`
